@page "/docs/extensions/video"

<Seo Canonical="/docs/extensions/video" Title="Blazorise Video component" Description="Learn how to use the Blazorise Video component to play local or streaming media with configurable sources, playback controls, responsive sizing, and browser-friendly markup." />

<DocsPageTitle Path="Extensions/Video">
    Blazorise Video component
</DocsPageTitle>

<DocsPageLead>
    Play local files or streaming media with the <Code>Video</Code> component.
</DocsPageLead>

<DocsPageParagraph>
    To use the <Code>Video</Code> component, install the <Code>Blazorise.Video</Code> package first.
</DocsPageParagraph>

<DocsPageParagraph>
    The extension uses Video.js v10 for browser playback. Its JavaScript, styles, streaming integrations, and skin assets are served from the package and loaded on demand, so normal usage does not require CDN references.
</DocsPageParagraph>

<DocsPageSectionTitle>
    Structure
</DocsPageSectionTitle>

<Table>
    <TableHeader>
        <TableRow>
            <TableHeaderCell>Type</TableHeaderCell>
            <TableHeaderCell>Purpose</TableHeaderCell>
        </TableRow>
    </TableHeader>
    <TableBody>
        <TableRow>
            <TableRowCell><Code>Video</Code></TableRowCell>
            <TableRowCell>Hosts the player, coordinates playback state, and exposes controls, events, streaming, and DRM options.</TableRowCell>
        </TableRow>
        <TableRow>
            <TableRowCell><Code>VideoSource</Code></TableRowCell>
            <TableRowCell>Describes the media type, title, poster, media files, and text tracks used by the player.</TableRowCell>
        </TableRow>
        <TableRow>
            <TableRowCell><Code>VideoMedia</Code></TableRowCell>
            <TableRowCell>Defines one media URL, MIME type, and optional dimensions. Multiple entries can represent selectable quality levels.</TableRowCell>
        </TableRow>
        <TableRow>
            <TableRowCell><Code>VideoTrack</Code></TableRowCell>
            <TableRowCell>Defines captions, subtitles, chapters, descriptions, or metadata associated with the media.</TableRowCell>
        </TableRow>
    </TableBody>
</Table>

<DocsPageSectionTitle>
    Installation
</DocsPageSectionTitle>

<DocsPageSection>
    <DocsPageSectionHeader Title="NuGet">
        Install the Video extension package.
    </DocsPageSectionHeader>
    <DocsPageSectionSource Code="VideoNugetInstallExample" />
</DocsPageSection>

<DocsPageSection>
    <DocsPageSectionHeader Title="Imports">
        Add the extension namespace to the application's main <Code>_Imports.razor</Code>.
    </DocsPageSectionHeader>
    <DocsPageSectionSource Code="ImportVideoExample" />
</DocsPageSection>

<DocsPageSection>
    <DocsPageSectionHeader Title="Runtime assets">
        No service registration, script tag, stylesheet link, or CDN reference is required. Blazorise loads the locally packaged Video.js core, styles, and the media adapter required by the current source.
    </DocsPageSectionHeader>
</DocsPageSection>

<DocsPageSection>
    <DocsPageSectionHeader Title="YouTube and Vimeo hosting requirements">
        Pass a regular public YouTube or Vimeo page URL to <Code>Source</Code>. The component detects the provider and creates the corresponding Video.js media element. The provider video must allow embedding and the browser must be able to reach that provider.
    </DocsPageSectionHeader>
    <UnorderedList>
        <UnorderedListItem>
            A restrictive Content Security Policy must include <Code>https://www.youtube.com</Code>, <Code>https://www.youtube-nocookie.com</Code>, and <Code>https://player.vimeo.com</Code> in <Code>frame-src</Code>. YouTube playback also requires <Code>https://www.youtube.com</Code> in <Code>script-src</Code> for its IFrame Player API.
        </UnorderedListItem>
        <UnorderedListItem>
            Private videos, videos whose owner disabled embedding, and provider restrictions such as age, region, or authentication requirements cannot be bypassed by the component.
        </UnorderedListItem>
        <UnorderedListItem>
            Content blockers can block the provider iframe or YouTube API even though all Blazorise and Video.js package assets are served locally.
        </UnorderedListItem>
    </UnorderedList>
</DocsPageSection>

